---
source: crates/nage/tests/cli.rs
expression: transcript
---
$ nage --help
[stdout]
Household accounting

Usage: nage <COMMAND>

Commands:
  serve    Run the web server until it is stopped; it updates the database first, after a backup
  health   Ask the server on this machine whether it is healthy; exit 0 only when it is
  init     Set Nage up at the terminal: the book, its currency and the first user, an admin
  user     Add a user or reset a user's password at the terminal
  check    Check that the book keeps every rule
  migrate  Update the database to this version of Nage, after a backup
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

The deployment guide for this version:
  https://github.com/bngoller/nage/blob/v[version]/docs/deploy.md
Report a problem:
  https://github.com/bngoller/nage/issues/new?template=problem.yml&version=[version]
[stderr]
[exit] 0
